# Coordinates for the marked M₁₂ Sylow subgroup

The three permutations `leftI`, `rightI`, and `movingActor * leftI * movingActor`
generate the actual common Sylow subgroup of the marked parabolic pair.
A breadth-first search supplies 64 words and their multiplication table.
The kernel checks distinctness and multiplication by the three generators;
induction on words then verifies the full multiplication table. The checked
cardinality in `SylowGeometry.Counts` proves that these coordinates exhaust
the actual subgroup, and hence that its homomorphisms are determined by the
three generators.

The tables are untrusted data, with all their uses justified by the proofs
below. The marked permutations and their source attribution are inherited
from `SmallParabolicPair.Seeds` (Aschbacher–Smith, Hypothesis 14.2.1 and
Lemma 14.2.21). These coordinates support the Sylow automorphism calculation
used in the outer-group inspection on printed p.510 and GLS3, Table 5.3b.
-/
